{"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference"],"title":"Related Documentation"},{"anchor":"How-to-Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"title":"How-to Guides","generated":true}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddpersistence"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence"},"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Add Persistence","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"abstract":[{"text":"Persist your domain entities to SwiftData with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro — no hand-written ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" classes, database actors, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closures.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" turns persistence into a declare-and-register concern. You annotate a domain entity with "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; the macro generates its SwiftData "},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" “shadow” class, the value↔model converters, and the "},{"code":"PersistableEntity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance. A generic "},{"code":"EntityDB","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" actor and a "},{"code":"PersistenceCoordinator","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" build the container, synthesize one "},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" per registered "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and reuse the core "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for debounced, batched writes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your reducers mutate plain value-type entities inside an "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"; the plugin observes the changelog and writes through to SwiftData after a debounce. Reads happen once, at launch, into memory — the in-memory "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is the source of truth."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For low-level manual wiring (writing your own "},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". For the macro details, see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". To add cross-device iCloud sync on top, see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Before-you-start","level":2,"text":"Before you start","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide assumes a Swidux app already exists — "},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"AppAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"AppReducer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"AppStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are wired and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If not, follow "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a local-only persistence layer. It needs "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no iCloud, CloudKit, or Push entitlements"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — only the sandbox "},{"code":"com.apple.security.network.client","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entitlement if your app also makes network calls (killswitch, analytics, feature flags). Adding sync entitlements to a local-only app is dead configuration and an App Review risk."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency","level":2,"text":"Step 1: Add the dependency","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the "},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" product to your app target in "},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxPersistence\",","    ]",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Step-2-Annotate-your-domain-entity-with-Persisted","level":2,"text":"Step 2: Annotate your domain entity with `@Persisted`","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A persisted entity is a value type that already satisfies "},{"code":"Identifiable & Equatable & Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"ID == UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" contract). Add "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiduxPersistence","","@Persisted","nonisolated struct Card: Identifiable, Equatable, Sendable {","    var id: UUID","    var quote: String","    var createdAt: Date","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This generates a "},{"code":"CardModel: @Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" class with "},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"toDomain()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"update(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", plus "},{"code":"extension Card: PersistableEntity { typealias Model = CardModel }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". By default every stored property is mirrored directly onto the model — SwiftData persists scalars "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" composites natively, so no manual blob columns are needed."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generated model is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CloudKit-safe by construction"}]},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"same"}]},{"type":"text","text":" model backs both the local and the synced container (see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"). SwiftData’s CloudKit mirroring requires every non-optional attribute to be optional or carry a default value, and every relationship to be optional — validated when the "},{"code":"ModelContainer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is created. "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" satisfies this automatically:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-optional mirrored attributes get a default."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" If you wrote one on the domain property (","type":"text"},{"code":"var count: Int = 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), it is propagated verbatim; otherwise the macro fills a canonical default for the known SwiftData primitives (","type":"text"},{"code":"String → \"\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Bool → false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", integers\/floats ","type":"text"},{"code":"→ 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date → .distantPast","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data → Data()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"UUID → UUID()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). Defaults are inert locally — ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" overwrites them on every load.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-primitive, non-optional properties"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (a custom ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type, ","type":"text"},{"code":"URL","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", an enum) have no default the macro can invent. Give the property a default (","type":"text"},{"code":"= …","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), make it optional, or mark it ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Inline","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — otherwise ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" emits a compile-time error.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Relationships are generated optional"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"var tags: [TagModel]? = nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"); a non-optional to-one ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Relation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a compile-time error (CloudKit forbids non-optional relationships).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Inline"},{"type":"text","text":" blob columns"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" default to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type is CloudKit-safe through ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Inline","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Because ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is never decodable, a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"non-optional"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Inline","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property must also carry a domain default (","type":"text"},{"code":"= …","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") — the generated getter falls back to it when the blob is missing or undecodable (e.g. a row CloudKit materialized before the blob synced). Omitting the default is a compile-time error (","type":"text"},{"code":"inlineRequiresDefault","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lives on the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"entity"}]},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lives on "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state containers"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" slices). They are different layers and never apply to the same type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Marker-macros-for-non-trivial-properties","level":3,"text":"Marker macros for non-trivial properties","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A macro can’t infer relationships, foreign keys, or which fields are derived. Four property markers (named to avoid SwiftData’s own "},{"code":"@Relationship","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"@Transient","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") tell "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" what to do:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Persisted","nonisolated struct Card: Identifiable, Equatable, Sendable {","    var id: UUID","    var quote: String","","    @Inline var styling: TextStyling = TextStyling()  \/\/ one opaque JSON Data column","    @ForeignKey var deckID: UUID                      \/\/ scalar parent reference","    @Relation(deleteRule: .cascade, inverse: \\TagModel.card)","    var tags: [Tag]                                   \/\/ SwiftData relationship","    @Ignored var renderedPreview: String?             \/\/ derived; omitted from the model","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Marker"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effect"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"(none)","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mirror the property directly (SwiftData persists scalars and "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" composites)."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Inline","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Force a "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value into a single JSON "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" column (keeps a CloudKit record compact; sidesteps SwiftData "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"-attribute edge cases)."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@ForeignKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Intent marker on a "},{"code":"UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; functionally a mirrored scalar column."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Relation(deleteRule:inverse:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A SwiftData relationship to another "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entity. The property’s type references the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"domain","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" type ("},{"code":"[Tag]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"Tag?","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"Tag","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"); the model substitutes the "},{"code":"…Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" shadow. "},{"code":"inverse","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a key path on the generated model, e.g. "},{"code":"\\TagModel.card","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"code":"deleteRule","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"code":"SwiduxDeleteRule","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":".cascade","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".nullify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".noAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".deny","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Ignored","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exclude a derived\/denormalized property. Must be optional so it can be reconstructed as "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on load."}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does not generate an "},{"code":"@Attribute(.unique)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — CloudKit forbids unique constraints. Identity is enforced by upsert-by-"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" inside "},{"code":"EntityDB","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the same generated model works for both local and synced containers."}]}],"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside"},{"anchor":"Step-3-Put-the-EntityStore-on-your-state","level":2,"text":"Step 3: Put the `EntityStore` on your state","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    var cards: EntityStore<Card> = .init()","    \/\/ ... your other slices","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your reducers mutate "},{"code":"state.cards","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" like any "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"state.cards[card.id] = card","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"state.cards.modify(id) { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"state.cards[id] = nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Every change is recorded for the plugin to drain."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Step-4-Build-the-coordinator-and-register-the-plugin","level":2,"text":"Step 4: Build the coordinator and register the plugin","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In "},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", build a local container, create a "},{"code":"PersistenceCoordinator","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", register its plugin, and run first-load hydration before constructing the store:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiduxPersistence","","extension Store where State == AppState, Action == AppAction {","    static func configured() async -> AppStore {","        let container = try! ContainerFactory.makeLocalContainer(models: [CardModel.self])","","        let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","            entities: [.entity(\\.cards)],","            container: container,","            debounce: .milliseconds(250)","        )","","        let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","        \/\/ Register UndoPlugin first if you use it — snapshots must precede writes.","        plugins.register(persistence.corePlugin)","","        var initial = AppState()","        await persistence.hydrate(into: &initial)   \/\/ first-load: fill EntityStores from disk","","        return Store(initialState: initial, reducer: { … }, plugins: plugins)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"hydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"first-load only"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — it replaces each "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" with the on-disk rows before any live edits exist. The only refresh path after launch is "},{"code":"rehydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which always "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"merges"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (preferring in-memory values) so a “refresh from disk” can never clobber unflushed writes or in-progress UI edits."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Surfacing-failures","level":3,"text":"Surfacing failures","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every save and fetch failure is logged, and the coordinator accepts an optional "},{"code":"onFailure:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" handler to additionally surface it to your app (a failed "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"save"}]},{"type":"text","text":" means the in-memory data is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" on disk; a failed "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"hydrate fetch"}]},{"type":"text","text":" leaves that "},{"code":"EntityStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" untouched rather than presenting an unreadable store as “no data”):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","    entities: [.entity(\\.cards)],","    container: container,","    onFailure: { failure in","        \/\/ e.g. dispatch an action that shows a \"couldn't save\" banner","    }",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Step-5-Flush-on-background","level":2,"text":"Step 5: Flush on background","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Writes are debounced, so drain them when the app is backgrounded or terminates:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".onChange(of: scenePhase) { _, phase in","    if phase == .background {","        Task { await persistence.corePlugin.flush() }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Multiple-entities-and-ordering","level":2,"text":"Multiple entities and ordering","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Register one "},{"code":".entity(\\.keyPath)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" per "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","    entities: [.entity(\\.decks), .entity(\\.cards), .entity(\\.tags)],","    container: try! ContainerFactory.makeLocalContainer(","        models: [DeckModel.self, CardModel.self, TagModel.self]","    )",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass every generated "},{"code":"…Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type to the container’s "},{"code":"models:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Writers flush in registration order — if entity B holds a "},{"code":"@Relation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to A, register A’s entity first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Testing","level":2,"text":"Testing","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The whole stack runs against an in-memory SwiftData store, so persistence is unit-testable with no disk and no CloudKit:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let container = try ContainerFactory.makeInMemoryContainer(models: [CardModel.self])","let db = EntityDB(modelContainer: container)","","try await db.upsert(Card(id: id, quote: \"hi\", createdAt: .now), as: CardModel.self)","let all = try await db.fetchAll(CardModel.self)","#expect(all.first?.quote == \"hi\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To prove the rule-#8 merge guarantee, seed the store, make a live in-memory edit, call "},{"code":"coordinator.rehydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and assert the live edit survives."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type